# The public-surface corpus: one minimal fixture per public rule, macro and
# aspect exported by the ten entry points listed in `exports_test.dart`.
#
# `bazel build //flutter/tests/corpus:all` builds every host-compatible
# fixture. Apple and Windows fixtures are skipped here by their platform
# constraint (or by the `manual` tag the public macro already gives them);
# they stay declared so that an `aquery` on their host sees their graph.
#
# The checked-in `actions.golden.json` covers the targets in
# `golden_targets.txt`; every other public fixture is in `uncovered_golden.txt`
# with the missing host capability. `exports_test` enforces both directions.
#
# The golden is Linux-x64 specific: it holds `flutter_linux-x64` and
# `llvm-toolchain-minimal-linux-amd64` repository paths, so regenerate it on a
# Linux-x64 host. From the repo root:
#
#   1. golden_targets.txt: list the labels
#      `bazel cquery --keep_going --skip_incompatible_explicit_targets
#      --output=label 'kind(rule, //flutter/tests/corpus:all) except
#      kind("dart_binary|dart_test|test_suite|cc_.*", //flutter/tests/corpus:all)'`
#      prints (sorted, deduplicated), minus the labels whose
#      `providers(target)` hold `IncompatiblePlatformProvider`.
#   2. actions.golden.json:
#      `bazel aquery --skip_incompatible_explicit_targets --output=jsonproto
#      "set($(grep -vE '^\s*(#|$)' flutter/tests/corpus/golden_targets.txt))"
#      > /tmp/flutter_corpus_aquery.json`, then
#      `bazel run //flutter/tests/corpus:actions_golden --
#      /tmp/flutter_corpus_aquery.json`.
